<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Province of Castellón</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Province of Castellón is the northernmost province of the Valencian Community in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, with its capital at Castellón de la Plana. It stretches from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast to the mountains of El Maestrat. In antiquity its northern part belonged to the Iberian Ilercavones, and in the 13th century it was conquered from the Muslims by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/province-of-castellon.jpg" alt="Province of Castellón" width="320" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castellon_in_Spain_(plus_Canarias).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
